{"born":[{"text":"b95b3aad94","mother":21,"rewritten":false},{"text":"240bca6a68","mother":14,"rewritten":true,"failure":null,"why":"The code improves survival by distinguishing between \"poisonous\" (leave/carries penalty) and \"unknown\" (taste/eat based on hunger) states, using a threshold of 2 experiences to form a belief, and switching to immediate consumption when starvation is imminent.","ms":7159},{"text":"b95b3aad94","mother":9,"rewritten":false},{"text":"5072304145","mother":17,"rewritten":true,"failure":null,"why":"The code prioritizes survival by tasting when hungry and avoiding clearly poisonous fruits, while carrying safe ones to eat later, adapting to learned traits rather than relying solely on instinct.","ms":4122},{"text":"fc798616de","mother":12,"rewritten":true,"failure":null,"why":"Prioritize survival by eating immediately when starving, then distinguish safe from poisonous fruits using a simple feed/harm ratio to confirm safety before committing to full consumption or seeking them again.","ms":4194},{"text":"b95b3aad94","mother":15,"rewritten":false},{"text":"b95b3aad94","mother":17,"rewritten":false},{"text":"89d172e021","mother":21,"rewritten":true,"failure":null,"why":"The code prioritizes survival by eating when starving, avoiding confirmed poison, carrying known good food for safety, and cautiously tasting novel fruits only when not desperate.","ms":6415},{"text":"b95b3aad94","mother":3,"rewritten":false},{"text":"b95b3aad94","mother":13,"rewritten":false},{"text":"779e9db165","mother":19,"rewritten":true,"failure":null,"why":"The code prioritizes survival by avoiding fruits with a history of poisoning (harm > safe) while aggressively eating known-safe fruits when hungry; it uses tasting only for novel items when hunger is low enough to afford the risk, and forces risk-taking on high hunger to avoid starvation.","ms":5403},{"text":"b95b3aad94","mother":5,"rewritten":false},{"text":"b95b3aad94","mother":21,"rewritten":false},{"text":"b95b3a